# Project structure

Top-level code lives under `src/`:

| Path | Holds |
|------|--------|
| `src/domain/` | Business logic, shared domain types, constants, providers |
| `src/ui/` | TUI only (Bubble Tea views, styles, list rendering) |
| `src/utils/` | Helpers reused from **more than one** place |

CLI entry (`main` / `cmd`) stays outside these folders and only wires domain + ui.

## Colocation

Related code that is **not** reused across the project stays in the **same feature folder**. Do not move types or helpers into a global `types/` or `utils/` just because they are types or helpers.

```text
# ✅ GOOD — feature-local types and helpers
src/domain/package_scripts/
  provider.go
  types.go      # only used here
  parse.go      # only used here

# ❌ BAD — splitting one feature across global buckets
src/domain/types/package_scripts.go
src/utils/parse_package_json.go   # only package_scripts needs it
```

## When to use `utils`

Promote to `src/utils/` only when a **second** caller needs the same helper (e.g. fuzzy filter used by every provider flow).

## Boundaries

- `src/ui` must not contain provider matching or `package.json` / filesystem business logic.
- `src/domain` must not render the TUI; it returns suggestions (`label`, `detail`, `value`).
